From ca2fe8fbbd7239de2bb745184d37d73c4b107617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sky Lift Group <usamash1010@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 22:13:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 1: render every page to static HTML, fix FAQ and mobile
 defects
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The site shipped as a client-only SPA: every route's HTML was ~5.9KB of head
tags wrapped around an empty <div id="root">. Google can render JavaScript but
queues it, and most AI/answer-engine crawlers (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot)
do not render it at all — so to them all 31 pages were blank. That is the
largest single reason pages sat crawled-but-not-indexed.

Static rendering
- Extract the route table into src/routes.jsx so the browser app and the build
  share one copy and cannot drift.
- Add src/entry-server.jsx (StaticRouter) and render every route at build time
  with React 19's prerender(), which resolves the lazy() route chunks instead of
  emitting Suspense fallbacks. The rendered markup is written into #root.
- Keep react/react-dom external in the SSR build. Bundling them produced a
  second React copy and "invalid hook call"; leaving the CJS deps external
  produced a module namespace object where a component was expected, which made
  the render fail silently and fall back to a blank page. noExternal + an
  explicit React external is the combination that works.
- The prerender step now fails the build if any route renders with no
  meaningful content, so a blank page cannot ship again unnoticed.

Result: pages now serve 242-2449 words of real HTML with no JavaScript.

FAQ answers were invisible to crawlers
- /faq and the homepage FAQ section only mounted an answer while its accordion
  item was open, so the HTML contained six questions and zero answers. Answers
  are now always in the DOM and collapsed by height. /faq went from 164 to 275
  rendered words, and FAQ schema (Phase 2) will now describe text that is
  actually on the page.
- Accordion buttons got aria-expanded/aria-controls, and the /faq questions are
  now h2 rather than span.

Mobile
- Sections animating in from `x: 40` sat 40px right of the viewport until
  scrolled into view, giving /contact and several service pages a horizontal
  scrollbar on a phone. html/body now use overflow-x: clip — clip rather than
  hidden so the page does not become a scroll container and break the sticky
  header.

Duplicate host
- skylift-group.vercel.app served the entire site on a second hostname with no
  redirect. It now 308s to the canonical www host, same as the apex already did.

Tooling
- scripts/audit-seo.mjs rewritten to crawl dist/ with no JavaScript and report
  titles, descriptions, canonicals, h1s, word counts, schema, broken internal
  links, orphans and sitemap disagreement, failing on anything critical.
- scripts/smoke-test.mjs added: loads routes in Chromium at desktop and phone
  widths and checks hydration, h1 count, horizontal overflow and JSON-LD
  parsing. Run with `npm run test:smoke`.
- Maintenance page moved back to a lazy import so it stays out of the main
  bundle while maintenance mode is off.

Verified: audit reports 0 critical / 0 broken links / 0 orphans / 0 duplicate
titles or descriptions; 20/20 page loads clean across desktop and mobile.

